1.Manhattan distance is defined as absolute difference between the measures in all dimensions of two points.It is also called a taxicab norm, or city block distance,
since calculating the distance between points resembles travelling in a taxi in square blocks of Manhattan.The name "Manhattan" is derived from the grid layout of most 
streets in Manhattan Island.The shortest path a car could take between two intersections in Manhattan streets has a length equal to intersection.

2.In KNN, if the euclidean distance of a data point from different centroids is equal,assign data point to cluster with less variance after adding data point.

3.KNN aims to create clusters having maximum inter(between) cluster variance or distance and minimum intra(within) cluster variance or distance.
